{
  "meta": {
    "site": "https://github.com/zengfr/n8n-workflow-all-templates",
    "tokenfree": "https://tokenyep.com/",
    "name": "Send webpage change alerts with Browserless, Google Drive, Gemini and Gmail",
    "wechat": "youandme10086",
    "id": 19449,
    "update_time": "2026-09-27"
  },
  "name": "Monitor a webpage for changes and email Gemini-described alerts",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "trigger",
      "name": "Check on a schedule",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.scheduleTrigger",
      "position": [
        0,
        208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "rule": {
          "interval": [
            {
              "field": "hours",
              "hoursInterval": 6
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.2
    },
    {
      "id": "overviewNote",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -864,
        -560
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 612,
        "height": 696,
        "content": "## Webpage change watcher with AI alerts\n\nChecks a public URL on a schedule, takes a screenshot with Browserless, and asks Gemini to compare it to the last one. You only get an email when something real changed, not when an ad rotated or a timestamp ticked over.\n\nScope: works on public pages, no login needed. Cookie banners are fine, Gemini is told to ignore that kind of noise. If a page needs a login or has a popup blocking the content, you'll need to customize the screenshot step (see the note next to 'Capture current screenshot').\n\nBefore running:\n1. Open 'Configuration' and set your target URL, a Drive folder ID, and where alerts should go.\n2. Add credentials for Browserless, Google Drive, Gmail and Gemini.\n3. Check the Gemini model on 'Compare screenshots with AI' (2.5 Flash is enough for this).\n4. First run creates the state table automatically.\n5. Run it once by hand to set the baseline, then turn on the schedule.\n\nWorth checking before you activate: the url field on the screenshot node, and the response field name on the Gemini node. Community nodes sometimes rename fields between versions, so it's worth a quick look."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "config",
      "name": "Configuration (edit this first)",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.set",
      "position": [
        224,
        208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "options": {},
        "assignments": {
          "assignments": [
            {
              "id": "1",
              "name": "targetUrl",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "https://example.com/pricing"
            },
            {
              "id": "2",
              "name": "driveFolderId",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "root"
            },
            {
              "id": "3",
              "name": "notifyEmail",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "you@example.com"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 3.4
    },
    {
      "id": "setupNote",
      "name": "Setup note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -32,
        -64
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 428,
        "height": 216,
        "content": "### 1. Setup & capture\nEdit Configuration first, it holds everything you need to change. The state table gets created on its own. Browserless grabs the screenshot, Drive stores it with a timestamp so you end up with a visual history over time."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "advancedNote",
      "name": "Advanced note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        544,
        -160
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 356,
        "height": 316,
        "content": "### Needs a login or has a popup blocking the page?\nThe Screenshot operation just loads the URL as-is, nothing fancier. If the page needs a login, has an age gate, or something's covering the content, switch this node to Browserless's 'Run Function' and write a short Puppeteer script that logs in or closes the popup first. That part is site-specific, so it's not built into the template, you'll need to add it yourself if your page needs it."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "ensureTable",
      "name": "Ensure state table exists",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "position": [
        464,
        208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "columns": {
          "column": [
            {
              "name": "url"
            },
            {
              "name": "last_screenshot_id"
            },
            {
              "name": "last_checked_at",
              "type": "date"
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "createIfNotExists": true
        },
        "resource": "table",
        "operation": "create",
        "tableName": "site_watch_state"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.1
    },
    {
      "id": "screenshot",
      "name": "Capture current screenshot",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-browserless-api.browserless",
      "maxTries": 3,
      "position": [
        688,
        208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "url": "={{ $('Configuration (edit this first)').item.json.targetUrl }}",
        "options": {},
        "operation": "screenshot",
        "additionalFields": {}
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000
    },
    {
      "id": "uploadDrive",
      "name": "Archive screenshot to Drive",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleDrive",
      "maxTries": 3,
      "position": [
        912,
        208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "name": "=Screenshot - {{ $('Configuration (edit this first)').item.json.targetUrl }} - {{ $now.toFormat('yyyy-MM-dd_HHmm') }}.png",
        "driveId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "My Drive"
        },
        "options": {},
        "folderId": {
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ $('Configuration (edit this first)').item.json.driveFolderId }}"
        }
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 3000
    },
    {
      "id": "checkFirstTime",
      "name": "Check: first time watching this URL?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "position": [
        1120,
        48
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "filters": {
          "conditions": [
            {
              "keyName": "url",
              "keyValue": "={{ $('Configuration (edit this first)').item.json.targetUrl }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "matchType": "allConditions",
        "operation": "rowNotExists",
        "dataTableId": {
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "site_watch_state"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.1
    },
    {
      "id": "checkReturning",
      "name": "Check: seen this URL before?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "position": [
        1120,
        368
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "filters": {
          "conditions": [
            {
              "keyName": "url",
              "keyValue": "={{ $('Configuration (edit this first)').item.json.targetUrl }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "matchType": "allConditions",
        "operation": "rowExists",
        "dataTableId": {
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "site_watch_state"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.1
    },
    {
      "id": "branchNote",
      "name": "Branch note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        976,
        -208
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 500,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "### 2. First run vs. every run after\nThe Data Table's row exists/not exists check splits the flow. First time seeing a URL, it saves a baseline screenshot and emails you to confirm. After that, every run compares against whatever was saved last time."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "saveBaseline",
      "name": "Save first screenshot as baseline",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "position": [
        1344,
        48
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "columns": {
          "value": {
            "url": "={{ $('Configuration (edit this first)').item.json.targetUrl }}",
            "last_checked_at": "={{ $now.toISO() }}",
            "last_screenshot_id": "={{ $('Archive screenshot to Drive').item.json.id }}"
          },
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow"
        },
        "options": {},
        "dataTableId": {
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "site_watch_state"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.1
    },
    {
      "id": "notifyBaseline",
      "name": "Email: baseline captured",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.gmail",
      "maxTries": 3,
      "position": [
        1568,
        48
      ],
      "webhookId": "d9c3ae85-b0c1-4bf5-b191-ff3d87ae3959",
      "parameters": {
        "sendTo": "={{ $('Configuration (edit this first)').item.json.notifyEmail }}",
        "message": "=I've captured the first screenshot of {{ $('Configuration (edit this first)').item.json.targetUrl }} as a baseline and saved it to Drive. I'll email you here when something meaningful changes.",
        "options": {},
        "subject": "=Watching started: {{ $('Configuration (edit this first)').item.json.targetUrl }}"
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "waitBetweenTries": 3000
    },
    {
      "id": "getPrevious",
      "name": "Look up last screenshot ID",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "position": [
        1344,
        368
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "limit": 1,
        "filters": {
          "conditions": [
            {
              "keyName": "url",
              "keyValue": "={{ $('Configuration (edit this first)').item.json.targetUrl }}"
            }
          ]
        },
        "matchType": "allConditions",
        "operation": "get",
        "dataTableId": {
          "mode": "name",
          "value": "site_watch_state"
        }
      },
      "typeVersion": 1.1
    },
    {
      "id": "downloadPrevious",
      "name": "Download previous screenshot",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.googleDrive",
      "maxTries": 3,
      "position": [
        1568,
        368
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "fileId": {
          "mode": "id",
          "value": "={{ $json.last_screenshot_id }}"
        },
        "options": {},
        "operation": "download"
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "typeVersion": 3,
      "waitBetweenTries": 3000
    },
    {
      "id": "combineImages",
      "name": "Combine current and previous images",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        1792,
        368
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const current = $('Capture current screenshot').item.binary.data;\nconst previous = $input.item.binary.data;\nreturn [{ json: $input.item.json, binary: { current, previous } }];"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "compareImages",
      "name": "Compare screenshots with AI",
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.googleGemini",
      "maxTries": 3,
      "position": [
        2000,
        368
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "text": "These are two screenshots of the same webpage. The first image is CURRENT, the second is PREVIOUS. Compare them and ignore trivial differences such as rotating ads, timestamps, cookie banners, or minor cosmetic pixel noise. If there is a meaningful content change (price, availability, status, new or removed text, a new listing, etc.), reply starting exactly with 'CHANGED:' followed by one plain-English sentence describing what changed. If there is no meaningful change, reply with exactly 'NO_CHANGE'.",
        "modelId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "mode": "list",
          "value": "models/gemini-2.5-flash",
          "cachedResultName": "models/gemini-2.5-flash"
        },
        "options": {},
        "resource": "image",
        "inputType": "binary",
        "operation": "analyze",
        "binaryPropertyName": "current,previous"
      },
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000
    },
    {
      "id": "compareNote",
      "name": "Compare note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1728,
        608
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 640,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "### 3. Comparing and alerting\nGemini looks at both screenshots and ignores cosmetic stuff. The state always updates, so each run compares against the most recent screenshot, not the very first baseline. You only get an email when it finds an actual change."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "updateState",
      "name": "Update last-checked state",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.dataTable",
      "position": [
        2224,
        368
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "columns": {
          "value": {
            "last_checked_at": "={{ $now.toISO() }}",
            "last_screenshot_id": "={{ $('Archive screenshot to Drive').item.json.id }}"
